\details{
A point is covered when \code{spec@engine} is \code{"auto"}, the method is
\code{\link[=reml]{reml()}} or \code{\link[=ml]{ml()}} on the observed information, the model is one that
\code{\link[=engine_model]{engine_model()}} describes, the family carries its derivatives to the
fourth order in the registry, and every penalized unit is a quadratic
penalty or a gaussian prior with a fixed mean and no map. The compiled
context computes, at the mode, the derivatives of the log-density to the
fourth order on the link scale, the observed information, the penalized
information pinned at \code{\link[=pinned_coords]{pinned_coords()}} with its inverse, the matrix of
the traces and the leverages, as the evaluation context of
\code{\link[=outer_context]{outer_context()}} holds them. Where the R route would take a branch that
the compiled context does not reproduce (a curvature that is not finite,
a Cholesky factor that fails or whose condition is within a factor of 100
of the acceptance threshold of \code{\link[=pd_factor]{pd_factor()}}, and therefore the
eigendecomposition and the retry over \code{\link[=deficient_coords]{deficient_coords()}}), the context
reports it and the R route computes the point. The context is stored in
